  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Establishment of a National Camp Coordination and Camp Management (CCCM) Mobile Team to Support and Improve Living Conditions at Informal Settlements and Ensure Evidence Based Durable Solutions Planning and Implementation</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In Afghanistan, a large number of internally displaced persons (IDPs) are settled at informal settlements, usually in public or private land. Forced eviction of IDPs living in informal settlements is a major risk particularly for those who have been displaced, in some cases, for more than 20 years and have re-built their life in the locations of displacement. The objective of this project is to establish a national, trained camp coordination and camp management (CCCM) mobile team to conduct assessments supporting principled decision making of sustainable solutions for IPDs and facilitate the coordination of services provision according to the Camp Management Standards in informal settlements. In addition, IOM is supporting the CCCM Working Group by covering any new displacement to an informal settlement, established as consequence of evictions and secondary displacements or other extreme events, such as drought, floods, earthquakes, poverty, and ongoing scattered conflicts, ensuring that a dedicated rapid CCCM response is available whether a CCCM actor is present or not.</narrative>
  </description>
